    "details": "NLnet Labs reports:\n\n> - CVE-2026-109140: Krill login-session tokens reuse their encryption\n>   nonce across restarts, so any user who can log in can forge an\n>   \\\"admin\\\" token.\n> - CVE-2026-109141: Krill users restricted to one CA can make any other\n>   CA delegate its prefixes and publish ROAs for them via bulk import.\n> - CVE-2026-109142: Krill treats a \\\"local parent\\\" as\n>   already-authenticated, letting a CA operator act as any child of any\n>   CA on the same server.\n",
